WEBVTT

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.520
It's almost summer break, huh?

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.170
I wanna go somewhere far away
on my bike over break.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.710
Spend a night and stuff.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.060
Yeah, let's go somewhere far!

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.330
You'll come too, right, Rin-chan?

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.700
Well...

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.590
I was thinking of going on a journey
to find myself during the summer...

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.380
But if you insist.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:26.960
Bike gangs aren't my thing.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.720
For all that she says, she always
comes with us anyway.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:50.230
この坂を上り切ったら
kono saka o noborikittara

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:54.200
必ず見える景色が好きだって
kanarazu mieru keshiki ga suki datte

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:54.240
必ず見える景色が好きだって

00:00:54.240 --> 00:01:00.370
背中に羽を持つあの子も言って笑ってた
senaka ni hane o motsu ano ko mo itte waratteta

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:04.040
ドキドキが一瞬で
dokidoki ga isshun de

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.130
トキメキになっていくんだなんて
tokimeki ni natteikunda nante

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:11.840
あの頃は信じられなくて
ano koro wa shinjirarenakute

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.800
ただ見惚れていたよ
tada mitoreteita yo

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:21.430
このスピードに乗せた体温が
kono supiido ni noseta taion ga

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:25.180
今全身で伝う　通じ合う
ima zenshin de tsutau tsuujiau

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.810
物語の鍵はこの手に
monogatari no kagi wa kono te ni

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:32.320
ぎゅっと強く握っているから
gyutto tsuyoku nigitteiru kara

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.030
感じて　応えて　風になる
kanjite kotaete kaze ni naru

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.700
空に溶けて海を抱きしめる
sora ni tokete umi o dakishimeru

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.620
新しい世界が見えるはず
atarashii sekai ga mieru hazu

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:50.710
さぁ確かめに行ってみよう
saa tashikame ni ittemiyou

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:04.100
Episode 4
Hot Springs!!

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.520
Come in.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.560
Excuse us!!

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.560
Please excuse us!

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.400
It's a mess, but make yourselves at home.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.610
Time to eat!

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.740
Time to eat.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.040
It's so sweet!

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.750
While we're on break, we could
go on a trip on our bikes.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.460
But where should we go?

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.000
What, Rin?

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.840
We should of course
go to Hokkaido

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.760
Oh, Hokkaido!

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.630
Hokkaido, huh?

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.340
But didn't you want to go
to "find yourself"?

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.930
Actually,

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.680
When I was little, I went there on a bike.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.390
But there's an ocean right?

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.190
How do you get across?

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.440
By ferry. There's one that leaves from Ibaraki.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.820
Rin-chan, what's Hokkaido like?

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.400
Roads that seem to never end...

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.570
Genghis Khan mutton...

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.860
Sapporo ramen...

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.490
Red foxes...

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.280
And the super long Seikan Tunnel.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.000
For having actually been there
you sound like a brochure.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.420
I was still little. Of course
I don't remember it that well.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.380
Can you even bike through the Seikan?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.090
No, trains only.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.130
When you're able to remember,
please tell me more.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.430
You went on that Katana, right?

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:24.220
I've never been there, either.
I'm interested to know.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.890
Alright, I'll try to remember.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.770
I think, first, we took the ferry

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.690
from Oarai, Ibaraki to Tomakomai.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.860
It's Hokkaido!

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.280
We're gonna get something to eat first.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.370
I'm so full from that grilled lamb!

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.790
Rin, we're gonna go to Sapporo first.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.840
Let's go have real Sapporo ramen!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.670
Hey, look Papa!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.510
There's a fox family on the road.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.670
Look, look!

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.680
Papa? Why are you heading towards them?

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.220
Turn! Turn! Turn!

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.350
Papa! Are you okay?

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:18.650
Rin, bikes go towards where you're looking...

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:19.820
Daddy!

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.030
Mr. Fox...

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.700
That tickles.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:34.330
So he was taken to the hospital in an ambulance,
and our trip to Hokkaido ended like that.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.170
This is all you've seen of Hokkaido?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.670
Yes, that's all! So sue me!

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:42.300
Maybe if we go to Hokkaido,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.470
By
Hane
yip!
Thank you,
Clock tower
Maybe if we go to Hokkaido,

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:48.470
the foxes you saved will remember
you and return the favor.
Clock tower
Thank you,
yip!
By
Hane

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.230
I feel like ripping that drawing apart.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.480
Eh? Is it?

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.270
It's cute, right, Hijiri-chan?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.690
Indeed.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.650
To tear up such a cute drawing

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.820
is what a lowly creature would do.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.150
Huh?

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.950
I feel like the foxes

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.370
did do something in return

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.120
some kind of gift...

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.620
Your father's sickness is called echinococcus.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.380
It appears he got it from foxes.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.420
It's a parasite.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.170
He needs surgery, so please sign here.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:27.220
Rin, the doctors say it'll be fine

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.800
but I know

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.890
It's probably over for me.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.560
Go home alone.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:37.980
Papa! Papa!

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.900
The Seikan Tunnel is so dark...

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.780
It's so long...

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.030
If you see a fox on the road

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.740
run it over!!

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.120
That's so cruel!!

00:05:55.450 --> 00:06:00.630
Renegades should be good
to their friends <i>and</i> animals!!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.800
You're just a villain, Rin!!

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.010
In that case,

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:12.850
why don't we all be renegades?

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.850
Let's ride our bikes
and go do bad things!!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.860
Let's go eat some midnight ramen!!

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.940
<b>She was called on her cell phone.</b>

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.820
<b>Shinya Ramen</b>

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.240
I'll get fat...

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.240
We're such delinquents.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.080
<b>Oarai</b>

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.620
How can you mistake a 18:30

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.920
for 8:30?!

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.210
None of you noticed, either!
You're just as guilty!

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.340
Even so, it doesn't seem like we'll make it...

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.760
I had trouble seeing the time
because I'm farsighted,

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.090
but still, this is the biggest mistake of my life.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.890
I can see Port Oarai!

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:56.810
The ship's still there!

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:00.350
The ship's already moving!

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.360
Whoa, not again...

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.030
Raimu-senpai!

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.790
She wants us to jump, too?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:18.950
Like we can do that!

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.960
This 750 is a monster, miss.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.170
There's nothing that a 1200cc bike

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.760
can do that this 750 can't.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.050
Those larger bikes sure are amazing...

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.430
I never could have survived in Siberia

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.810
if I couldn't make a jump like this one.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.310
Hayakawa...

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.230
I'm guess I'm not young anymore.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.920
I'll go get a new bike, and I'll join up with you guys.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.640
Don't force yourself.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.350
Let's meet in Hokkaido, tomorrow.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:25.560
Let's ride!

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:28.110
There's a ferry from Aomori to Hokkaido.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.980
Let's go now!

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.190
What are you saying, Hane?

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.530
Aomori is still 700 kilometers away.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.070
What about you, Onsa-chan?

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.910
Really?

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.830
As for me, as long as we ride, it's fine.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.880
or rather, deep within my heart is
a burning desire to ride.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:52.670
Do you even realize how far it is, Shaggy?

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:54.630
Do you know how long it'll take us?

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.140
Rin, do you know what "The Cannonball" is?

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.430
It's an American Crosscountry Race
that's also a comedy.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:05.810
That race has actually been run in Japan.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.060
A race from Tokyo to Hokkaido.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.190
The Cannonball is an endurance.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.240
An inner struggle.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:20.280
Everyone being at their limit to keep going.
and when they arrive at Hokkaido,

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:25.580
at the first cup of coffee in the morning,
all those riders find out what it truly means to ride a bike.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.750
Yes, this is romance.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.750
So you're in, right?

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.260
Don't say I didn't warn you.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:37.930
All right! We're going to Aomori!

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.480
If we keep going like this,
we'll never make it.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:49.060
Besides, with your slow Serow
there's no way we can keep going at this pace.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:49.900
What?

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.820
Fine, wanna do a race to Aomori?!

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.360
Try and catch up!

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.030
Let's Cannonball!

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.320
Hey, wait!

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:07.080
Looks like I feel behind.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.960
It's nice that the road is empty but..

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.210
but it's dark and I feel lonely.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:17.220
My hands are going numb,
my butt hurts, and I'm about to passout.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:21.430
I probably would've been
better just to wait for the next ferry.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.270
But it's too late.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.270
I wonder how they're doing?

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.570
This blinky pattern...

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.370
I'm about to run out of fuel!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.330
I need to find a gas station!

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:47.330
Huh?

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:49.620
Someone's pulled over with a bike.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.420
Is there anything wrong?

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.090
Running out of gas sure is a pain.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:06.350
Well, I only have a liter left.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.560
Let's split it.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:08.640
Are you sure?

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:13.270
I'm not sure, but if we run out again
we can help each other out.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:17.530
But, I'm sure god will help us
reach the next gas station!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.160
By the way, your bike's a Harley, right?

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.120
How cool!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:27.040
No, it's a Suzuki Intruder.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.460
Oh, is that so?

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.040
We're saved.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:35.960
Thank God.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:36.670
Sure.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.420
Huh?

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:40.340
God loves bikes.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.010
He does?

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:45.350
In Ezekiel 1 of the Old Testament,

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:50.180
there's mention of the Lord
arriving on a wheeled vehicle.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.310
Occultists say it was a UFO,

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:59.110
but here's a depiction painted
by Raphael 500 years ago.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.990
I don't see any wheels.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.490
But with the help of modern X-ray analysis,

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:09.870
science has discovered the original
drawing that was hidden beneath.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.500
This looks just like Rin-chan's bike!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:18.500
Raphael understood the Lord's vehicle,

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.510
but since there was no conception
of bikes at the time,

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.510
he painted animals over it instead.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:29.140
Just as God loves humanity for its weakness,

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.890
He loved motorcycles.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.850
For motorcycles, too, were weak vehicles.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:40.780
Something about the way this guy
talks reminds me of Onsa-chan.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:45.490
Bikes are the weakest of all
vehicles in this world.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.700
They cannot carry people
or cargo the way cars can,

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.290
and by carrying another rider behind you,

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.580
the joy of the bike is lost.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.830
They are not as economical

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.000
or healthful as bicycles.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.880
The tires are vulnerable
to potholes and manholes.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:06.510
Should a bike fall over, it breaks
down under its own weight.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.890
Oh, is it running out of gas?

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:12.810
Well, no problem, I'll just
switch to my reserve tank...

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:19.570
Crap! I'm already on reserve!

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:21.650
I'm really out of gas!

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:24.530
Fool!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.780
By the Sisterhood Code,
I'm leaving you behind.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:29.660
This is a race, get used to it!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.580
If you are not strong, you cannot ride a bike.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:40.460
And...

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.010
If you are not kind,

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.970
you cannot continue to ride.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:50.850
Now, let us go.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:51.970
Ah, yeah.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.520
I know a shortcut to Aomori.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:56.810
I'll take you there.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.350
Really?

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:02.020
First, I must thank you for the gasoline.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.440
It's alright.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:12.080
The cup of immortality, sought by King Arthur
and his Knights of the Round Table...

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:13.830
The Holy Grail.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.950
For you, the chosen one.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.890
I... fell asleep?

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.350
I wonder where this is?

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.770
Could I be...

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.940
Excuse meee, is this Heaven?

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.570
Not at all.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.360
This here is Aomori.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:48.030
Oh... I see.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.280
<b>Aomori Port</b>

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.670
Coffee to stay awake.

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.170
And then the bathroom.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.540
And right after that more coffee.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:05.130
Restroom... Coffee...

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.050
Restroom... Coffee... Restroom...

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.090
Romantic.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:10.760
I'm sorry.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:14.600
Until Hane comes, I'm taking a nap.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.770
Hey, look.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.860
You guys are late!

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:26.230
Hane?

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.650
How in the world did you get ahead?

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:30.740
I guess it's a miracle!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:38.330
<b>Hakodate Port</b>

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:46.460
We're in Hokkaido!

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:51.340
Hijiri said she's be waitng for us
at Hakodate with her new bike.

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.890
I'm so sorry for the long wait.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.390
Hijiri-chan!

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.110
Red, red,

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:11.400
red bodies, with L, L,

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.820
L-shaped twins...

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:18.410
We're the awesome Ducatists!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:20.500
Oh, how unusual.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:24.170
A roundcase 750SS Imola.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:26.340
You keep it in gorgeous shape.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.880
But why a side car?

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.050
This is a crime against Ducati!

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.380
What a waste of a perfectly beautiful bike.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:34.720
Despicable.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.100
Your Desmosedici is much better, Kinzo-san.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.390
Uh-huh, it cost 8 million.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.980
Wow!

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.390
Where's the the little boys' room?

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:48.110
Oh, dear. Now I need to go, too.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:04.670
TL Note: If a bike is standing upright,
it will retract the stand.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.290
It's just like you talked about, Hayakawa.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:09.630
Indeed.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.460
Ducatis have souls.

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:18.550
I'm tired.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:23.140
We were on our bikes all day
but it took 4 hours to get back on a ferry.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:25.140
I guess we're living our youth!

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.650
I wanna just take a shower
and go to sleep.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.320
The shower's broken.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.690
What?!

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:34.240
I'm just gonna go to sleep.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:38.070
In Hakodate, I hear there's
a marvelous hot spring.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.700
We could go first thing in the morning.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.500
I'm done.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:44.870
Let's sleep.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.120
Huh? Did we forgot something?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:49.210
Oh, yeah...

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:50.790
Aren't we forgetting something?

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:55.670
We left Raimu-senpai at Tomakomai!

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.610
A hot spring so close to the ocean!

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.240
What the heck? You can
completely see it from the outside.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.700
And it's a mixed bath?

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.040
This is too much!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.700
It's fine.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.500
Raimu-senpai!

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.180
We're such renegades!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.110
I guess Hane tricked us all.

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:55.280
Now that I'm in here
it's pretty nice.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.190
I've never felt so free.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:01.910
I did not think we would pass through Hakodate
on our path to Tomakomai.

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.870
What a pleasant surprise.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.710
This feels so good!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.630
Rin-chan, is that...

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:22.720
What?

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:28.930
What the heck?!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:29.770
Huh?

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:32.600
Didn't ya get yourself branded?

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.480
Of course not!

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.780
This is... This is...

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:44.410
Hey, Papa, do the thing.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.410
All right, here it comes!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:46.200
Jackknife!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.700
Whee!
Jackknife!

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:48.040
Whee!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.000
How's that?

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:49.870
Huh?

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.790
Whee!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:52.790
Man, kids sure do fly far.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.000
Whee!
Man, kids sure do fly far.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:55.210
Man, kids sure do fly far.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:58.300
I made a carbon-fiber-textured emblem myself.

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.220
Whoa, the hood's hot!

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.340
Hey, this thing's backwards.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.010
You're right.

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.430
Suzuki drivers are going
to think you're an idiot.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.180
Whee— Ow!

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:15.520
I can't get married
with a butt like this!

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:19.860
Rin-chan, in this world there's definitely

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:23.780
a guy somewhere with a Suzuki
branding on his butt.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.740
No, there isn't.

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:27.910
I don't want a man like that!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.250
I can't believe all of you!

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.210
What is it, Hayakawa?

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:37.340
I'd never dreamed that such a time would come.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:41.210
High-school girls touring together on bikes,

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:43.970
and bathing together in an open hot spring...

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.510
Such a time.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:49.470
It seems that my last duty in
this life will be to have you,

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:52.980
a lady who has never even ridden a bicycle,

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.350
get a bike license.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.820
Hayakawa, please refrain
from being so morbid.

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:01.780
But I sense it.

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:04.610
The moment my Ducati breaks down

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:08.280
is the moment my life ends.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:16.960
What happened?

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:19.380
Oh, it's not a big deal.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:21.760
Is everything all right?

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:25.430
It would seem the Aftermarket
Cub's are malfunctioning.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:27.930
"Made in Japan" doesn't
mean quality anymore, huh?

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:28.850
Such a liar.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:32.430
Huh?

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:36.850
My...

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:43.150
Miss Hijiri.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:44.900
It is fixed this quickly?

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:50.030
I had thought the engine blew up.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.700
That's nonsense.

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.250
Ducatis never break down.

